+++ b/viewer/README.md
@@ -44,6 +44,31 @@ WINDOWS
 Unzip SillViewer-windows.zip anywhere. Run "Sill Viewer.exe". Keep the DLL files next to it.
 Windows asks once to let it through the firewall: allow it on private networks.
 
+WINDOWS KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS FOR A MAC
+In the stream window, turn on "Mac shortcuts (Ctrl → ⌘)", then click the picture.
+Ctrl+Q quits the Mac app, Ctrl+W closes its window, Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+T opens a tab,
+and Ctrl+C/X/V/A/Z send the corresponding Command shortcuts. Shift and Alt keep their
+usual meanings (Shift and Option). The choice is saved separately for each paired host.
+
+Turn the option off for native Mac Control shortcuts (for example, Ctrl+C to interrupt
+a terminal command) or when connecting to Linux. It is off for a new host. The Windows
+logo key is not captured or remapped, and Windows shortcuts such as Alt+Tab remain local.
+Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F still controls the viewer's full screen mode. The mapping does not
+apply to local viewer controls, including the pairing code and address fields.
+
+Keys are released on focus loss, disconnect, quitting, or a mapping change. To change
+the option while full screen is on, leave full screen with Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F first.
+
+BUILD THIS CHANGE FOR WINDOWS
+The manual "Windows with Mac shortcuts" GitHub Actions workflow runs the keyboard
+checks, builds the Windows executable and packages it with its DLLs. In your fork,
+open Actions, choose that workflow, click "Run workflow", then download the
+SillViewer-windows-mac-shortcuts artifact from the completed run. It contains
+SillViewer-windows.zip; extract that zip before running the executable.
+
+Keyboard checks alone (no FFmpeg or display required):
+  cargo test --locked --manifest-path tests/keyboard/Cargo.toml
+
 MAC
 In Terminal, in this folder:   ./build-mac.sh
 It installs Homebrew's ffmpeg and Rust if needed, builds "Sill Viewer.app" and puts it in
